# Generated and machine-local parts of the layout editor.
#
# Only what is rebuilt on demand, or is not ours to ship, is ignored. Anything
# the editor needs as *input* is kept however large: the point of this folder is
# that anyone can clone it and build a ship without hunting down assets.

# Module thumbnails and turntable renders, rebuilt by the server on first
# request, plus its own logs. ~51 MB.
tool/cache/

# Saved layouts are scratch copies; the ship the tool actually reloads is
# export/ship_manifest.json.
tool/layouts/

# Each suite drops a screenshot at the end of its run, purely to be looked at.
# Tracked once, they turned into binary churn in every diff: `npm test`
# rewrites all three whether or not anything changed.
tool/test/shot-*.png

# The exported ship: a 38 MB .glb rebuilt from the manifest by Save, and the
# timestamped backups the server keeps on every write. Those backups
# are ignored here but are NOT expendable on disk - they are the recovery path,
# and they have already been the only thing that got work back. The live
# manifest itself is NOT ignored (it is the ship), and neither is
# ship_collision.json, which is the kit's hulls and is meant to travel, nor
# ship_compounds.json, which is the compound library and travels with them.
export/*.glb
export/ship_manifest.*-*.json
export/ship_collision.*-*.json
export/ship_compounds.*-*.json
export/ship_autosave.*-*.json

# The captured environment probes: .env cubemaps the editor renders on demand,
# their stamps, and the index that records what was captured. Rebuilt by Capture
# from the ship itself, so they are outputs rather than inputs.
export/environments/

# The current recovery copy, rewritten every couple of minutes while you work.
# Never a deliberate save, so never part of the history.
export/ship_autosave.json

# The HDRI is a placeholder with no recorded provenance, and is not the one this
# ship will ship with - so it is not committed. The editor starts without it and
# says so ("no HDRI, metals will look flat"); only reflections suffer, because
# metals take nearly all their brightness from the IBL. Drop any .hdr in here
# and point ENV_HDRI (tool/public/js/editor.js) at it.
env/*.hdr

temp/

# Deliberately NOT ignored: export/ship_manifest.json,
# export/ship_collision.json and export/ship_compounds.json. Those three ARE
# the ship, its hulls and the pieces it is assembled from.
#
# The kit is no longer here at all. The modules are read from BabylonAssets -
# a local checkout of it, or https://assets.babylonjs.com, whichever
# tool/config.json selects - because they are not all CC0 and are not ours to
# redistribute. See license.txt.